bluegl: a linear one-level import keeps its own pitch (no 64-byte row rule),
so the GPU reads CoreAnimation's wrapped client images in place. GL imports only
(fdl_image_params.any_linear_pitch) and texels of 4 bytes or more: Turnip shares this
layout code and samples such images sheared (ca-draw -a8, -rgba).

